type-attachement {
    define at consumption, at definition, or implicitly: i.e. in the file, or at a reference, or by location.
    e.g.
       - an idea might say "i'm a x type", or
       - a reference might say - "i require this to be an x-type", or
       - a file might say - all ideas inside this file need to be x-types, or
       - a folder/project might say - all ideas inside this project/folder need to be x-types,
          - e.g. optional status attribute that is one of a set of literals
       - a combination - which is when an interesection is required.
}

